WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.110 --> 00:00:04.330
There are three things you probably fear reading
about these days.

00:00:04.330 --> 00:00:09.470
The outcome of your college midterm exams,
the daily news, and your gas and electric

00:00:09.470 --> 00:00:10.470
bill.

00:00:10.470 --> 00:00:13.080
For the first two, nothing to say: it happens.

00:00:13.080 --> 00:00:17.720
As for the rising bills, yes, that happens
too, but for specific reasons.

00:00:17.720 --> 00:00:18.930
And you’re not too wrong.

00:00:18.930 --> 00:00:23.760
When we talk about gas and electricity we
are referring to what provides us with a basic

00:00:23.760 --> 00:00:28.580
standard of living: heating, hot water, electricity
and gas for cooking.

00:00:28.580 --> 00:00:31.130
In short, your domestic hearth.

00:00:31.130 --> 00:00:35.870
Not to mention, of course, those factories
who cannot work without gas and electricty.

00:00:35.870 --> 00:00:41.990
Let's start with the harsh reality: the entire
European Union is not self-sufficient in energy,

00:00:41.990 --> 00:00:44.900
which means a dense network of imports.

00:00:44.900 --> 00:00:50.190
Of course, if Norway was an EU country, we
might consider it an anomaly: over there they

00:00:50.190 --> 00:00:52.040
produce plenty of gas.

00:00:52.040 --> 00:00:57.210
One hundred and one billion cubic meters of
gas in 2020 (BP plc)...which they don't even

00:00:57.210 --> 00:00:58.210
use.

00:00:58.210 --> 00:01:03.579
They make do with only 4 billion, since they
manage to get by with hydroelectricity and

00:01:03.579 --> 00:01:04.640
burning churches.

00:01:04.640 --> 00:01:10.100
In fact, in 2020 they exported something like
one hundred and ten billion cubic meters of

00:01:10.100 --> 00:01:11.100
gas.

00:01:11.100 --> 00:01:13.560
There is actually a European champion for
gas production.

00:01:13.560 --> 00:01:15.010
Or rather there was.

00:01:15.010 --> 00:01:20.360
We're talking about the Netherlands, which
a decade ago was around 70 billion cubic meters

00:01:20.360 --> 00:01:21.390
of gas produced.

00:01:21.390 --> 00:01:27.430
There’s a small problem however: a bit like
the Dwarves of Moria, the Dutch have dug too

00:01:27.430 --> 00:01:30.840
deep, causing seismic damage related to drilling.

00:01:30.840 --> 00:01:35.170
The large Groningen plant will close soon
but the production has already been drastically

00:01:35.170 --> 00:01:38.420
reduced down to 20 billion cubic meters.

00:01:38.420 --> 00:01:44.229
And If there's a fourth thing you would absolutely
not want to see, this is the map of the gas

00:01:44.229 --> 00:01:45.810
pipelines that cross the old continent.

00:01:45.810 --> 00:01:52.530
Where (and how) do these billions of cubic
meters of gas arrive in the homes of us Europeans?

00:01:52.530 --> 00:02:03.479
Non-European natural gas came 43.9% from Russia,
19.9% from Norway, 11.9% from Algeria, 5.5%

00:02:03.479 --> 00:02:11.700
from UK, 5.0% from USA and a remaining 13.8%
from other countries such as Azerbaijan, Qatar,

00:02:11.700 --> 00:02:14.310
Libya, Nigeria, Trinidad and Tobago.

00:02:14.310 --> 00:02:19.780
These are the main countries that extract
and sell their gas to us today, both in natural

00:02:19.780 --> 00:02:22.930
form and LNG, i.e. liquefied gas.

00:02:22.930 --> 00:02:27.510
The undisputed queen, or rather the czarina,
is Russia.

00:02:27.510 --> 00:02:31.980
Much of the gas exported to the old continent
is extracted from the fields of the Yamal

00:02:31.980 --> 00:02:33.989
peninsula in northwestern Siberia.

00:02:33.989 --> 00:02:39.410
It is here that we find the famous "taps",
more precisely near the pleasant town of Novyj

00:02:39.410 --> 00:02:40.410
Urengoy.

00:02:40.410 --> 00:02:41.640
And here the mess begins.

00:02:41.640 --> 00:02:46.970
From Novyj urengoy the Northern Lights pipeline
starts and proceeds unhindered to the town

00:02:46.970 --> 00:02:49.670
of Torzhok, north-west of Moscow.

00:02:49.670 --> 00:02:55.680
Here two things happened: the pipeline continued
towards Belarus, on the Smolensk-Minsk directive,

00:02:55.680 --> 00:03:01.630
where it split: one part continues north,
towards Lithuania and then Kaliningrad, another

00:03:01.630 --> 00:03:04.920
part south, towards western Ukraine.

00:03:04.920 --> 00:03:10.220
At Torzhok, the Northern Lights pipeline also
joins a second pipeline, the Yamal-Europe,

00:03:10.220 --> 00:03:15.840
which passes through Minsk and Poland to the
German border at Lebus, where it joins the

00:03:15.840 --> 00:03:17.100
German JAGAL system.

00:03:17.100 --> 00:03:22.830
The Urengoy-Pomary-Uzghorod, known as the
Brotherhood, also departs from Novyj Urengoy,

00:03:22.830 --> 00:03:30.180
a 4,400 km long snake that crosses the Ukraine
and reaches the Slovakian border, in parallel

00:03:30.180 --> 00:03:33.190
with the Soyuz, which departs to the south,
from Orenburg.

00:03:33.190 --> 00:03:38.090
On the one hand, there's Belarus, through
which the gas that feeds Germany and therefore

00:03:38.090 --> 00:03:43.379
north-western Europe passes, and on the other,
there's Ukraine, the gateway through which

00:03:43.379 --> 00:03:46.110
the traffic for Balkan and southern Europe
flows.

00:03:46.110 --> 00:03:47.470
But there is more.

00:03:47.470 --> 00:03:52.760
Yep, in fact, a branch of the Brotherhood
flows to Novopskov, in the Luhansk People's

00:03:52.760 --> 00:03:57.569
Republic, from which it then reconnects to
the Ukrainian network up to Kiev, crossing

00:03:57.569 --> 00:03:59.020
practically the whole country.

00:03:59.020 --> 00:04:04.310
But let's pretend that in donbass everything
is regular and no war is going on, there are

00:04:04.310 --> 00:04:08.510
other Russian routes that reach Europe bypassing
Ukraine and Belarus.

00:04:08.510 --> 00:04:13.599
Well, Europe up to a certain point if we talk
about the Turkstream pipeline, which from

00:04:13.599 --> 00:04:19.129
Anapa, on the shores of the Black Sea with
a privileged view on Crimea, sinks to reach

00:04:19.129 --> 00:04:25.009
Turkey, at Ipsala, where it evolves into Turkstream
2 running up the continent to Hungary.

00:04:25.009 --> 00:04:29.889
The same applies to the Blue Stream, which
crosses the Black Sea from the Izobilny plant

00:04:29.889 --> 00:04:31.430
to reach Ankara directly.

00:04:31.430 --> 00:04:36.340
The Anatolian corridor is of particular interest,
especially for us Italians, since we rely

00:04:36.340 --> 00:04:39.020
on around 40% on the Russian gas.

00:04:39.020 --> 00:04:45.069
We are talking about the Trans-Adriatic Gas
Pipeline, the TAP, active since the end of

00:04:45.069 --> 00:04:51.819
2020 that will connect Italy, more precisely
the receiving terminal of Melendugno in Apulia,

00:04:51.819 --> 00:04:56.439
straight to the rich field of Shah Deniz,
in Azerbaijan, on the coast of the Caspian

00:04:56.439 --> 00:04:57.439
Sea.

00:04:57.439 --> 00:05:02.750
The TAP passes through Albania and crosses
Greek Macedonia to Kipoi on the Turkish border.

00:05:02.750 --> 00:05:08.289
There it connects to TANAP, the Trans-Anatolian
Pipeline all the way to Georgia, where it

00:05:08.289 --> 00:05:12.499
finally attaches to the South-Caucasian Pipeline,
the end of this straw that feeds our country

00:05:12.499 --> 00:05:13.499
with Azeri gas.

00:05:13.499 --> 00:05:15.189
In 2021, 7 billion cubic meters passed through
Melendugno.

00:05:15.189 --> 00:05:19.630
But we’re not done with Russia: we need
to talk about Nord Steam.

00:05:19.630 --> 00:05:27.460
Active since 2011, Nord Stream creates a direct
supply line between Vyborg, Russia, and Greifswald,

00:05:27.460 --> 00:05:29.990
Germany, passing under the Baltic Sea.

00:05:29.990 --> 00:05:35.060
Attaching to the Gryazovets-Vyborg pipeline,
Nord Stream feeds some of the gas that passes

00:05:35.060 --> 00:05:36.659
through the Northern Light.

00:05:36.659 --> 00:05:41.350
Something like 55 billion cubic meters per
year can pass through Nord Stream, although

00:05:41.350 --> 00:05:46.509
some European sanctions on Gazprom have reduced
its actual capacity by half.

00:05:46.509 --> 00:05:48.849
What's the deal, let's just build another
one, right?

00:05:48.849 --> 00:05:53.759
In September, the controversial project of
Nord Stream 2 was completed, an almost parallel

00:05:53.759 --> 00:05:59.580
pipeline (instead of Vyborg it connects to
Ust-Luga) that would double the direct supply

00:05:59.580 --> 00:06:04.399
capacity of Germany from Russia with aroud
one hundred and ten billion cubic meters if

00:06:04.399 --> 00:06:05.719
all goes well.

00:06:05.719 --> 00:06:07.860
And why should anything ever go wrong?

00:06:07.860 --> 00:06:12.099
Well, the list of views against this Nord
Stream 2 is quite long.

00:06:12.099 --> 00:06:15.810
And then we should also consider that The
Nord Stream 2 company, based in Switzerland

00:06:15.810 --> 00:06:18.929
went bankrupt the day before yesterday.

00:06:18.929 --> 00:06:19.990
Thank you sanctions.

00:06:19.990 --> 00:06:24.400
First of all, the project contradicts the
common energy policy that the European Union

00:06:24.400 --> 00:06:29.529
is trying to pursue, diversifying its supplies
to free itself from Russian dependence.

00:06:29.529 --> 00:06:34.840
Russia, on the contrary, would see in the
potential of Nord Stream 1 and 2 an alternative

00:06:34.840 --> 00:06:39.199
channel to the compulsory steps of Belarus
and especially Ukraine.

00:06:39.199 --> 00:06:44.039
This would offer Moscow a fearsome weapon
of blackmail and influence on its neighbors.

00:06:44.039 --> 00:06:49.509
It is not only Ukraine that's involved, because
Slovakia, Hungary, Romania, Poland are all

00:06:49.509 --> 00:06:50.509
in this game...

00:06:50.509 --> 00:06:53.759
Putin could knock on Kiev's door and impose
his conditions.

00:06:53.759 --> 00:06:59.240
Otherwise: no more gas through Ukraine, because
me - Russia - can bring it straight to Germany.

00:06:59.240 --> 00:07:03.360
Diversification doesnt mean simply changing
course, but finding other suppliers.

00:07:03.360 --> 00:07:06.629
There is, however, another detail, rather
disturbing.

00:07:06.629 --> 00:07:13.020
The company that will operate the new pipeline,
Nord Stream 2 AG based in Switzerland is totally

00:07:13.020 --> 00:07:18.759
owned by Gazprom International Projects LLC,
a branch of Gazprom itself.

00:07:18.759 --> 00:07:24.280
Nord Stream 2 AG is all that remains of the
joint venture formed by, in addition to Gazprom,

00:07:24.280 --> 00:07:30.759
E.ON, Shell, Wintershall, OMV and Engie, a
consortium later blocked by the Polish antitrust

00:07:30.759 --> 00:07:31.770
authorities.

00:07:31.770 --> 00:07:37.509
These former partners are now outside Nord
Stream 2 AG, but they have given substantial

00:07:37.509 --> 00:07:39.289
amounts of money as "sponsors".

00:07:39.289 --> 00:07:44.119
The management of Nord Stream 2 by Gazprom
alone, in addition to giving even more centrality

00:07:44.119 --> 00:07:49.689
to Russia, would go against the European energy
policies that prevent suppliers from controlling

00:07:49.689 --> 00:07:52.029
the energy transmission networks.

00:07:52.029 --> 00:07:56.849
And one of the first nations to risk the consequences
of Nord Stream 2 is Poland.

00:07:56.849 --> 00:07:58.669
But Poland has already run for cover.

00:07:58.669 --> 00:08:03.399
Yes, because, fortunately for Europe, next
to the monopolized Baltic Sea there is another

00:08:03.399 --> 00:08:05.649
sea, rich in deposits: the North Sea.

00:08:05.649 --> 00:08:10.309
This year, work should begin on the Baltic
Pipe, a pipeline that will connect the northern

00:08:10.309 --> 00:08:15.349
coasts of Poland to the heart of the North
Sea, passing through Denmark, and attaching

00:08:15.349 --> 00:08:20.319
itself to the network with which Norway supplies
Western Europe and the United Kingdom.

00:08:20.319 --> 00:08:24.870
And here we come to our two "not too much
European country": What the UK and Norway

00:08:24.870 --> 00:08:28.949
have done in the North Sea may at first seem
like a complete mess.

00:08:28.949 --> 00:08:33.940
The North Sea is full of gas fields that the
two countries have long shared, but Norway

00:08:33.940 --> 00:08:39.209
also has rich deposits close to the Arctic,
in the waters north of Trondheim.

00:08:39.209 --> 00:08:44.940
As we have seen, Norway exports almost all
of the gas it extracts, and pipelines to the

00:08:44.940 --> 00:08:50.199
UK depart from the Arctic, such as the Langeled
pipeline to Loftus, on the coast of North

00:08:50.199 --> 00:08:54.860
Yorkshire, and the parallel Ormen Lange Field-Easington
pipeline.

00:08:54.860 --> 00:09:00.410
The coasts between Bergen and Stavanger represent
a real hub where gas extracted from the northern

00:09:00.410 --> 00:09:05.899
North Sea and the Arctic is redirected to
continental Europe, through pipelines such

00:09:05.899 --> 00:09:12.630
as Zeepipe (in Belgium) or Europipe II, which
connects Stavanger to the Dutch coast.

00:09:12.630 --> 00:09:17.100
Holland and Belgium are, however, largely
supplied by the many Norwegian extraction

00:09:17.100 --> 00:09:20.040
sites located in the southern waters of the
North Sea.

00:09:20.040 --> 00:09:22.880
And Then there is the United Kingdom, which
has some problems.

00:09:22.880 --> 00:09:28.370
It extracts plenty of gas compared to the
European average, in 2020 it was about 40

00:09:28.370 --> 00:09:34.800
billion cubic meters, but it consumed almost
twice as much, 72 billion according to Eurostat.

00:09:34.800 --> 00:09:38.829
The biggest problem, however, is the lack
of an adequate storage network.

00:09:38.829 --> 00:09:40.800
This is why UK has few supplies.

00:09:40.800 --> 00:09:47.029
This is also due to the shutdown of the Rough
plant in 2017, which alone for 30 years accounted

00:09:47.029 --> 00:09:50.730
for 70% of the country's storage capacity.

00:09:50.730 --> 00:09:55.410
In any case, there are 3 main hubs towards
which the flows of British gas and imported

00:09:55.410 --> 00:10:02.139
quotas from Norway are condensed: Aberdeen,
North Yorkshire and Bacton, in North Norfolk.

00:10:02.139 --> 00:10:06.560
From these three nodal points the UK national
network is supplied.

00:10:06.560 --> 00:10:11.850
This includes as well the three main terminals
from which LNG is exported and imported by

00:10:11.850 --> 00:10:17.649
sea: Milford Haven, in Wales, the Grain LNG
terminal, on the island of Grain, in Kent

00:10:17.649 --> 00:10:18.649
and in Middlesborough.

00:10:18.649 --> 00:10:23.120
For many, LNG is a solution to the excessive
dependence on Russian gas.

00:10:23.120 --> 00:10:28.930
A solution that is certainly more expensive
than transportation by pipelines, but more

00:10:28.930 --> 00:10:31.730
adaptable and no longer bound by geographical
proximity.

00:10:31.730 --> 00:10:34.550
But it does not have only positive aspects.

00:10:34.550 --> 00:10:40.370
Yeah sure, it is fine to replace Russia and
Nord Stream, but the arrival of ships loaded

00:10:40.370 --> 00:10:46.370
with LNG from the United States also has repercussions
on the honest Norwegian exporters.

00:10:46.370 --> 00:10:51.160
If the Russian pipeline policy is threatening
the European geopolitical and economic balance,

00:10:51.160 --> 00:10:53.519
the American involvement is no less.

00:10:53.519 --> 00:10:58.189
In the LNG routes not only the United States
are involved, of course.

00:10:58.189 --> 00:11:04.889
Spanish ports, Marseille, Rotterdam, Athens...these
are the main destinations of LNG coming from

00:11:04.889 --> 00:11:07.890
Qatar, Nigeria, Trinidad and Tobago.

00:11:07.890 --> 00:11:14.870
Even we Italians, so thirsty for gas, have
important LNG import terminals, in La Spezia,

00:11:14.870 --> 00:11:17.149
Livorno and in the Adriatic Sea.

00:11:17.149 --> 00:11:22.480
Adriatic Sea which is well supplied with fields
that are not much exploited by our workforce.

00:11:22.480 --> 00:11:28.410
After all, it looks awful to go to the sea
and see the Italian floating stations on the

00:11:28.410 --> 00:11:30.620
horizon, much better the Croatian ones, right?

00:11:30.620 --> 00:11:35.050
We Italians have also another interesting
rout in the Mediterranean Sea: in the heart

00:11:35.050 --> 00:11:39.839
of the Algerian desert lies the largest African
gas field: Hassi R'mel.

00:11:39.839 --> 00:11:45.209
This gas oasis is the starting point for three
very important gas pipelines for southern

00:11:45.209 --> 00:11:50.589
Europe: on the one hand, there are the two
Maghreb-Europe and Medgaz pipelines, which

00:11:50.589 --> 00:11:53.829
cross Morocco and the Mediterranean to supply
Spain.

00:11:53.829 --> 00:11:59.050
On the other, the Trans Mediterranean pipeline,
which crosses Tunisia and arrives in Sicily,

00:11:59.050 --> 00:12:03.829
at Mazara del Vallo, and then climbs the entire
peninsula, as far as Slovenia.

00:12:03.829 --> 00:12:07.749
From Libya, on the Tripoli-Gela route, comes
the Greenstream.

00:12:07.749 --> 00:12:13.160
There is also the interesting project of GALSI
(Gas Pipeline Algeria Sardinia Italy) that

00:12:13.160 --> 00:12:18.209
from the Algerian Gulf of Annaba should bring
gas to Sardinia and from there to Tuscany.

00:12:18.209 --> 00:12:20.730
But the southern route does not end in Africa.

00:12:20.730 --> 00:12:25.879
There has been talk for some years of a gas
pipeline, the East Med, which from the fields

00:12:25.879 --> 00:12:31.370
in the Eastern Mediterranean Sea between Cyprus
and Israel should run to Greece between Crete

00:12:31.370 --> 00:12:36.550
and the Peloponnese, and then it shoudl enter
our Adriatic Sea through the Poseidon pipeline,

00:12:36.550 --> 00:12:37.639
up to Otranto.

00:12:37.639 --> 00:12:42.589
Erdogan permitting: the Turks have different
views on Cyprus fields, as well as a different

00:12:42.589 --> 00:12:46.749
understanding of Exclusive Economic Zones
in the Mediterranean Sea.

00:12:46.749 --> 00:12:50.959
So we have come to the end of this exciting
trip up and down Europe.

00:12:50.959 --> 00:12:51.959
"Exciting".

00:12:51.959 --> 00:12:56.949
Rising bills could be a rather long-lasting
reality if certain measures are not taken,

00:12:56.949 --> 00:12:59.861
but I am certainly not the best person to
explain them to you.

00:12:59.861 --> 00:13:03.899
I leave you some links in the description,
so you can have a look at the European gas

00:13:03.899 --> 00:13:04.899
pipeline mess.

00:13:04.899 --> 00:13:06.360
This video could have been much worse.

00:13:06.360 --> 00:13:11.089
In the meantime I just say thank you for listening
to me until the end and see you next time.

00:13:11.089 --> 00:13:11.370
Ciao.

